      "Both platforms offer strong SEO capabilities, but BigCommerce generally provides more granular control over URL structures and other on-page SEO elements, which can be advantageous for advanced optimization strategies. Shopify's SEO is robust for most businesses, but its URL structure can be less flexible.",
      "Which platform is more cost-effective for a growing business?",
      "The cost-effectiveness depends on your sales volume and feature needs. Shopify's transaction fees can make it more expensive for high-volume stores if you don't use Shopify Payments. BigCommerce charges no transaction fees, which can lead to better margins for rapidly growing businesses, though its base plans might appear slightly higher for very small operations.",
      "Can I migrate my store from Shopify to BigCommerce (or vice versa)?",
      "Yes, both platforms support store migrations. You can use third-party migration tools, hire a migration service, or manually export/import data. The complexity and cost of migration depend on the size of your store, the number of products, customer data, and order history.",
      "Which platform is better for dropshipping?",
      "Shopify is often considered more popular for dropshipping due to its extensive app ecosystem, particularly integrations with dropshipping suppliers like Oberlo (now Dsers). Its ease of use also appeals to new dropshippers. BigCommerce can also support dropshipping, but may require more manual setup or different app choices.",
      "Do BigCommerce and Shopify offer B2B features?",
      "Yes, both platforms offer B2B capabilities. BigCommerce has more robust native B2B features built into its platform, including customer groups, wholesale pricing, and purchase orders. Shopify offers B2B functionality primarily through its Shopify Plus plan and various third-party apps.",
